WEBVTT

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:09.120
We're heading out, Admiral.

00:00:12.710 --> 00:00:14.530
We're all counting on you.

00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:19.240
Ooyodo, leave the rest to us.

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:21.940
I will, Yahagi-san.

00:00:23.290 --> 00:00:26.730
My beautiful catapult's still working.

00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:30.950
Yes. I have Zuiuns now.

00:00:30.950 --> 00:00:33.340
I'm all set. Don't worry.

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:38.300
Once you've loaded up 
the resources from the south...

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:39.890
I know.

00:00:39.890 --> 00:00:41.990
We leave the Zuiuns in Singapore.

00:00:41.990 --> 00:00:46.020
Our top priority is loading up and 
transporting strategic resources.

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:47.400
Right, Hyuuga?

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:49.280
Yes, that would be correct.

00:00:49.790 --> 00:00:51.180
I hate to leave them all behind,

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:55.130
but what's important now is to bring materials
 from the south back to the homeland.

00:00:55.130 --> 00:00:58.570
We'll leave the Zuiuns we're 
equipped with in Syonan.

00:00:58.570 --> 00:01:00.740
They'll be useful in defending that area.

00:01:01.490 --> 00:01:02.560
Thanks.

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:04.470
Leave it to us.

00:01:04.470 --> 00:01:05.710
Of course.

00:01:06.150 --> 00:01:08.750
Carrier Division 4, heading out!

00:01:09.180 --> 00:01:11.090
Roger. Let's go.

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:16.880
Operation Kita Completion 
Force, all ships, set sail!

00:01:17.360 --> 00:01:19.660
Our destination is Syonan, AKA Singapore!

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:33.440
It's all up to you now...

00:01:55.460 --> 00:02:02.120
<b>See You Again on Another Quiet Blue Sea</b>

00:03:22.970 --> 00:03:27.430
<b>Dark Clouds</b>

00:03:32.140 --> 00:03:35.360
From Torpedo Squadron 2, 
they took Kasumi and Asashimo.

00:03:35.730 --> 00:03:37.820
And there's Hatsushimo.

00:03:37.820 --> 00:03:40.120
Yes. Three ships.

00:03:40.810 --> 00:03:42.980
And the Light Cruiser, Ooyodo.

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:48.510
So, Yahagi will be both the admiral's 
secretary and head of Torpedo Squadron 2?

00:03:50.280 --> 00:03:51.820
Probably, yes.

00:03:53.630 --> 00:03:56.290
Shigure, are you servicing your 
anti-submarine equipment?

00:03:56.910 --> 00:04:00.120
Yeah, it's important.

00:04:02.030 --> 00:04:03.610
Now, especially.

00:04:04.660 --> 00:04:10.430
I heard that on her way back to the mainland, 
Kongou got hit by enemy subs.

00:04:10.800 --> 00:04:15.800
Fortunately, she made the wise decision 
to cut speed and withdraw to Taiwan.

00:04:16.270 --> 00:04:19.760
Yeah, she miraculously survived with moderate damage.

00:04:19.760 --> 00:04:22.100
But her escort, Urakaze...

00:04:23.750 --> 00:04:25.050
Isokaze...

00:04:25.840 --> 00:04:29.410
It's fine. Urakaze made it there, somehow.

00:04:30.140 --> 00:04:33.400
But for a destroyer, 
a direct hit with torpedoes is...

00:04:34.330 --> 00:04:36.020
She's alive.

00:04:36.020 --> 00:04:39.620
She was taken off the naval roster 
the other day, and left the military.

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:45.630
We have to do our best 
to protect the innocents we serve.

00:04:45.630 --> 00:04:48.340
Want to take a break, you two?

00:04:48.850 --> 00:04:51.230
Thanks, Hamakaze.

00:04:51.230 --> 00:04:52.560
Let's do that.

00:04:52.960 --> 00:04:55.740
Here you go. Rice balls and mikan oranges.

00:04:58.630 --> 00:05:00.400
Thanks!

00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:07.160
Yukikaze, you're always cheerful.

00:05:07.550 --> 00:05:10.870
Yup! Yukikaze is always cheerful!

00:05:25.890 --> 00:05:28.030
What's her problem?

00:05:28.710 --> 00:05:31.190
Yuki's always full of energy.

00:05:32.840 --> 00:05:36.970
You're close to her, Shigure?

00:05:36.970 --> 00:05:37.940
That's a surprise.

00:05:37.940 --> 00:05:41.470
No, I wouldn't say we're close.

00:05:44.270 --> 00:05:45.340
No?

00:05:54.590 --> 00:05:55.720
It's good.

00:06:03.100 --> 00:06:04.380
Oh, Shigure.

00:06:05.800 --> 00:06:08.620
Shigure, Ryuuhou is in port for repairs.

00:06:08.620 --> 00:06:10.850
Ryuuhou?

00:06:10.850 --> 00:06:13.570
She just came to report to the admiral.

00:06:13.570 --> 00:06:15.950
Thanks. I'll go see her.

00:06:18.990 --> 00:06:20.970
Thanks for the food, Hamakaze.

00:06:27.430 --> 00:06:30.030
She's pretty busy too, huh?

00:06:46.510 --> 00:06:48.970
Shigure, no running in the hallways.

00:06:50.210 --> 00:06:51.430
Sorry!

00:06:52.760 --> 00:06:54.180
What's gotten into you?

00:06:54.180 --> 00:06:56.930
Yahagi, did you see Ryuuhou? 
I heard she's in port.

00:06:56.930 --> 00:06:59.740
Oh, carrier Ryuuhou?

00:06:59.740 --> 00:07:01.400
She was just in the admiral's room—

00:07:01.400 --> 00:07:03.030
Thanks, Yahagi.

00:07:04.740 --> 00:07:06.440
No running in the hallways!

00:07:07.460 --> 00:07:08.820
Shigure!

00:07:16.370 --> 00:07:17.450
Ryuuhou!

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:20.370
Shigure.

00:07:20.730 --> 00:07:22.020
It's been so long.

00:07:22.670 --> 00:07:24.100
Ryuuhou.

00:07:24.100 --> 00:07:26.960
You look well, Shigure. I'm glad.

00:07:26.960 --> 00:07:29.250
When did you get to Sasebo?

00:07:29.250 --> 00:07:30.990
This afternoon.

00:07:30.990 --> 00:07:34.170
I was supposed to do a transport 
mission to the Philippines,

00:07:34.170 --> 00:07:36.930
but it got changed to Taiwan 
because of the state of the war.

00:07:37.580 --> 00:07:39.250
Transport mission?

00:07:39.930 --> 00:07:41.130
Carrying what?

00:07:42.370 --> 00:07:43.560
Shigure?

00:07:45.390 --> 00:07:47.860
Shigure, it's fine.

00:07:47.860 --> 00:07:48.960
Admiral?

00:07:50.190 --> 00:07:56.380
I'm having Ryuuhou carry the latest model 
of Suisei 33 land-based dive bombers

00:07:56.380 --> 00:07:59.160
to strengthen their air defenses.

00:07:59.160 --> 00:08:02.190
Yes. With the Kinsei engine.

00:08:02.620 --> 00:08:04.720
Oh, I see.

00:08:05.080 --> 00:08:06.530
Well, you know...

00:08:06.530 --> 00:08:10.020
They have an ultra-stable air-cooled engine.

00:08:28.280 --> 00:08:31.030
There's a lot of those lately.

00:08:31.030 --> 00:08:35.140
Yeah, the army's bringing in a ton.

00:08:36.210 --> 00:08:41.060
But with these additional planes, 
as well as ammo and repair parts,

00:08:41.060 --> 00:08:43.970
the area will be much better defended.

00:08:43.970 --> 00:08:44.870
Yes.

00:08:45.660 --> 00:08:48.460
I just talked to Yahagi,

00:08:48.460 --> 00:08:50.990
and we're sending four of Torpedo 
Squadron 2's best destroyers

00:08:50.990 --> 00:08:53.720
as escorts on this transport mission.

00:08:54.630 --> 00:08:56.080
From Torpedo Squadron 2, Shigure,

00:08:56.660 --> 00:09:02.360
Isokaze, Hamakaze, and Yukikaze 
will be participating!

00:09:03.310 --> 00:09:04.560
Yes, sir.

00:09:05.230 --> 00:09:07.180
I'm counting on you to be
 at your best, Shigure.

00:09:08.950 --> 00:09:09.980
Yes, sir.

00:09:10.920 --> 00:09:13.850
I'm glad to have you with me again, Shigure.

00:09:15.450 --> 00:09:17.460
Shigure, Torpedo Squadron 2.

00:09:17.460 --> 00:09:22.620
Alongside Isokaze, Hamakaze, and Yukikaze, 
I will serve as Ryuuhou's escort.

00:09:23.870 --> 00:09:26.000
A mission with Yuki...

00:09:28.120 --> 00:09:29.000
I'm counting on you!

00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:30.670
Thank you.

00:09:31.230 --> 00:09:32.040
Of course!

00:09:49.530 --> 00:09:51.020
Huh?

00:09:56.280 --> 00:09:58.190
My stomach...

00:10:04.980 --> 00:10:08.820
My stomach hurts!

00:10:25.690 --> 00:10:26.640
What?

00:10:29.150 --> 00:10:31.610
Yukikaze's got engine trouble?

00:10:31.610 --> 00:10:34.590
A really bad stomachache, it seems.

00:10:36.680 --> 00:10:40.740
Something about eating too 
many mikan oranges at once...

00:10:40.740 --> 00:10:44.540
Doesn't she realize we have a mission soon?

00:10:44.540 --> 00:10:45.890
Yuki...

00:10:45.890 --> 00:10:52.360
If it's bad, I'm told, they'll be sending her
back to Kure for a full engine overhaul.

00:10:57.570 --> 00:10:59.440
That Stupid girl!

00:11:01.310 --> 00:11:04.230
We'll have no choice but to send Ryuuhou

00:11:04.230 --> 00:11:08.140
with a three ship escort: 
Isokaze, Hamakaze, and Shigure.

00:11:09.340 --> 00:11:10.750
Three ships?

00:11:11.400 --> 00:11:13.720
We don't have any spare ships,

00:11:13.720 --> 00:11:15.560
and there's no time to waste right now.

00:11:16.180 --> 00:11:19.410
Don't worry. 
It's not just three destroyers.

00:11:19.410 --> 00:11:23.040
It's three of Torpedo Squadron 2's 
most veteran destroyers.

00:11:27.040 --> 00:11:29.380
Tomorrow at 0800,

00:11:30.100 --> 00:11:35.710
you are to leave port as Ryuuhou's escort.

00:11:36.420 --> 00:11:39.340
After seeing Ryuuhou safely to Taiwan,

00:11:39.340 --> 00:11:42.170
you are to link up with one of 
the Hi convoys in the region.

00:11:42.170 --> 00:11:44.830
You will serve as their escort, as well.

00:11:45.590 --> 00:11:46.910
Hi convoys...

00:11:47.640 --> 00:11:50.810
The convoy in question already 
has four coastal defense ships:

00:11:50.810 --> 00:11:56.840
Mikura, Kurahashi, Yashiro, 
and Coastal Defense Ship 30.

00:11:56.840 --> 00:12:00.120
But there are huge numbers 
of enemy submarines in the area.

00:12:01.540 --> 00:12:05.080
Sea lane protection is now every bit
 as important as the front lines.

00:12:05.080 --> 00:12:08.860
There's no way to win this except 
to have our fleet destroyers assist.

00:12:11.060 --> 00:12:14.140
It may just be an escort mission, but show 
them the strength of Torpedo Squadron 2!

00:12:14.140 --> 00:12:15.200
I'm counting on you!

00:12:16.270 --> 00:12:17.500
Roger.

00:13:13.220 --> 00:13:16.440
Shigure, Torpedo Squadron 2, 
ready to set sail.

00:13:16.980 --> 00:13:20.650
Torpedo Squadron 2, DesDiv 17, 
Hamakaze. Ready to go.

00:13:20.650 --> 00:13:26.290
Torpedo Squadron 2, DesDiv 17, 
Isokaze. Heading out!

00:13:26.290 --> 00:13:27.110
Follow me!

00:14:55.960 --> 00:14:58.180
Thanks again, Shigure.

00:14:58.580 --> 00:15:01.680
Yeah, leave it to us.

00:15:49.870 --> 00:15:53.160
I think it's going to rain. 
You okay, Shigure?

00:15:53.160 --> 00:15:54.940
I'm just fine.

00:15:56.220 --> 00:16:00.440
But... I don't like the way this feels.

00:16:01.370 --> 00:16:02.520
Isokaze!

00:16:02.920 --> 00:16:03.870
What is it?

00:16:03.870 --> 00:16:05.360
The radiolocator's picked up something.

00:16:05.760 --> 00:16:09.710
<i>I believe it to be radar waves 
from enemy submarines.</i>

00:16:10.140 --> 00:16:11.320
They're coming.

00:16:11.320 --> 00:16:13.280
Enemy radio transmission detected.

00:16:13.280 --> 00:16:14.630
It's unencrypted.

00:16:14.630 --> 00:16:15.570
Wait, more than one!

00:16:15.570 --> 00:16:17.190
They're not scared of us at all.

00:16:17.980 --> 00:16:19.790
And so close to the mainland...

00:16:19.790 --> 00:16:22.780
All ships, begin zig-zag maneuvers.

00:16:22.780 --> 00:16:25.640
Torpedo Squadron 2, prepare 
for anti-submarine combat.

00:16:25.640 --> 00:16:28.230
Be on the watch both above 
and below the surface.

00:16:31.090 --> 00:16:33.170
Multiple torpedo trails to the port side.

00:16:33.500 --> 00:16:35.510
Ryuuhou, evasive maneuvers.

00:16:35.510 --> 00:16:37.600
Starboard!

00:16:37.600 --> 00:16:41.310
Torpedo Squadron 2, 
begin anti-submarine combat!

00:16:46.100 --> 00:16:47.190
Shigure!

00:17:05.580 --> 00:17:06.790
Hamakaze!

00:17:06.790 --> 00:17:08.230
I see them!

00:17:14.100 --> 00:17:14.800
Hamakaze!

00:17:16.760 --> 00:17:19.120
Isokaze! Right side this time!

00:17:19.720 --> 00:17:22.680
We're surrounded. Wolf pack tactics?

00:17:31.660 --> 00:17:32.610
<i>Shigure!</i>

00:17:34.070 --> 00:17:35.240
Yamashiro?

00:17:47.370 --> 00:17:50.510
Shigure reporting. One enemy
 submarine down.

00:17:50.840 --> 00:17:52.110
Shigure!

00:17:52.550 --> 00:17:53.710
Nice.

00:17:53.710 --> 00:17:54.820
There!

00:17:59.390 --> 00:18:02.190
Isokaze reporting. One 
submarine sunk for sure!

00:18:02.970 --> 00:18:04.650
There are still multiple in the area.

00:18:04.650 --> 00:18:06.180
Be careful!

00:18:20.570 --> 00:18:21.860
Shigure!

00:18:24.080 --> 00:18:25.200
Take this!

00:18:50.470 --> 00:18:52.680
<i>What is it doing over there?!</i>

00:19:05.100 --> 00:19:07.560
<i>Am I going to sink?</i>

00:19:16.130 --> 00:19:17.340
Yamashiro!

00:19:29.000 --> 00:19:33.440
No rain lasts forever...

00:19:37.530 --> 00:19:38.540
Shigure!

00:19:38.690 --> 00:19:39.580
Shigure!

00:19:43.450 --> 00:19:46.570
I'm all out of depth charges.

00:19:46.910 --> 00:19:48.580
I have a few left.

00:19:49.250 --> 00:19:50.830
Shigure...

00:20:14.540 --> 00:20:18.490
Everyone. Ahead, at 12 o'clock.

00:20:19.530 --> 00:20:22.770
Coastal Defense Fleet, full speed ahead!

00:20:28.780 --> 00:20:29.880
The rain...

00:20:31.860 --> 00:20:34.000
Mikura-Class Coastal Defense Ship, Mikura!

00:20:34.420 --> 00:20:35.460
Kurahashi, too!

00:20:35.800 --> 00:20:36.920
I'm Yashiro!

00:20:36.920 --> 00:20:39.880
Type-C Coastal Defense Ship 30!

00:20:40.530 --> 00:20:42.830
We're here to help!

00:20:44.670 --> 00:20:48.550
Hi Convoy Escort Ships, 
Line Abreast Formation!

00:20:48.960 --> 00:20:50.180
Line Abreast!

00:20:50.180 --> 00:20:51.550
Roger!

00:20:53.660 --> 00:20:55.400
Prepare for Anti-Submarine combat!

00:21:00.940 --> 00:21:02.400
Fire!

00:21:23.020 --> 00:21:25.460
Nothing on radiolocator!

00:21:29.420 --> 00:21:30.660
Shigure...

00:21:45.250 --> 00:21:46.410
<i>The rain...</i>

00:21:50.400 --> 00:21:51.810
<i>stopped.</i>

00:21:51.810 --> 00:21:52.640
Good work out there!

00:21:52.640 --> 00:21:53.430
Are you okay?

00:21:53.430 --> 00:21:54.640
Sorry we're late!

00:23:28.760 --> 00:23:29.910
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:34.680 --> 00:23:39.980
<b>Naval Interception Mission</b>

00:23:35.180 --> 00:23:38.300
Interceptor Fleet, Torpedo 
Squadron 2, raising anchor!

00:23:38.300 --> 00:23:39.490
Let's go!
